      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "HITCH TO HIS STAR (9) raced wide in the latter stages but was too good at his latest appearance, recording a gutsy win by 1.3 metres at Melton. Draws for a trail and he has won four of six previous visits to this venue. Has the ability to collect the prize again. BUSINESS IN HEAVEN (8) had been working towards a win and it arrived in style last week, coming from the back row and getting home by 10.5 metres at this circuit and distance. Must overcome a very wide draw but could go on with it now. IDEAL TIMING (6) is close to a win after two successive seconds at Menangle, the latest from this barrier. Chance to break through. IMA BOXA (7) worked from a tough draw in the West Wyalong Cup last start and was solid when placed at Melton prior. His fitness is building and he has won two of his three previous attempts at this circuit and distance.",
